{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_1785849743733","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f97228c5133bdb4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp && python3 -c \"\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\nimport re\n\nclass TextExtractor(HTMLParser):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.text = []\n        self.skip = False\n    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):\n        if tag in ('script','style','nav','header','footer'):\n            self.skip = True\n        if tag in ('h1','h2','h3','h4','p','div','section','li','td','th','tr','table','figure','figcaption'):\n            self.text.append('\\n')\n    def handle_endtag(self, tag):\n        if tag in ('script','style','nav','header','footer'):\n            self.skip = False\n        if tag in ('p','div','section','h1','h2','h3','h4'):\n            self.text.append('\\n')\n    def handle_data(self, data):\n        if not self.skip:\n            self.text.append(data)\n\nwith open('swantale.html','r',encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    html = f.read()\n\next = TextExtractor()\next.feed(html)\ntext = ''.join(ext.text)\ntext = re.sub(r'\\n\\s*\\n', '\\n\\n', text)\ntext = re.sub(r' +', ' ', text)\n# Output from offset 50000 onward\nprint(text[50000:])\n\" 2>&1 | head -3000","description":"Extract remaining text from SwanTale HTML"}}],"model":"GLM-5.2-w4a8","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"584cd32d-8f5a-4355-a7a4-58219c9f0cec","uuid":"69e8af5a-99da-4254-861f-3e1c0a1b41ec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f97228c5133bdb4","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (59.6KB). Full output saved to: /inspire/qb-ilm/project/video-generation/chenxie-25019/hyr/iHateTheWorld555.github.io/.claude-review/projects/-inspire-qb-ilm-project-video-generation-chenxie-25019-hyr-iHateTheWorld555-github-io/584cd32d-8f5a-4355-a7a4-58219c9f0cec/tool-results/bwij2ip0q.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n=bmaxnull+(bminnull−bmaxnull)​q​(t),\\displaystyle=b_{\\max}^{\\mathrm{null}}+\\left(b_{\\min}^{\\mathrm{null}}-b_{\\max}^{\\mathrm{null}}\\right)q(t),\n\n(17)\n\nc​(t)\\displaystyle c(t)\n\n=cmin+(cmax−cmin)​q​(t).\\displaystyle=c_{\\min}+(c_{\\max}-c_{\\min})q(t).\n\n(18)\n\nThe vector 𝐛null​(t)\\mathbf{b}^{\\mathrm{null}}(t) takes bnull​(t)b_{\\mathrm{null}}(t) on the null-expert dimensions and zero on the routed-expert dimensions. A larger q​(t)q(t) yields a higher cumulative-probability threshold, a weaker preference for null routing, and greater expert capacity. A smaller q​(t)q(t) reduces additional expert transformations and shifts more computation toward task-shared and null paths at the same denoising stage.\n\nDynamic Top-PP routing with annealed Gumbel mixing.\nThe number of experts required varies substantially across frames. Stable backgrounds and near-silent regions typically require few additional transformations, whereas speaker changes, environmental sound fields, and superimposed global audio events may benefit from multiple experts. Fixed Top-KK routing assigns the same number of experts to every frame and cannot adapt to this variation. Unified MoE therefore uses dynamic Top-PP routing.\n\nDuring training, we first draw Gumbel noise for all routed audio and null experts:\n\ngℓ,m,i=−log⁡(−log⁡uℓ,m,i),uℓ,m,i∼𝒰​(0,1).g_{\\ell,m,i}=-\\log\\left(-\\log u_{\\ell,m,i}\\right),\\qquad u_{\\ell,m,i}\\sim\\mathcal{U}(0,1).\n\n(19)\n\nThe Gumbel-Softmax selection distribution is t